<!-- The folder’s outline, and the panel behind. The front covers all of it but the tab, so what
     this contributes is the tab and the left-hand sliver; it is kept whole so the two panels cannot
     drift apart, and so the outline stays one shape if the front ever moves.

     The corners are quarter circles, which is why the radius is not a number that can be edited on
     its own: both control points are fixed fractions of it, and every straight run between two
     corners gives up what the corners now take. The shoulder where the tab steps down keeps its
     angle, being a diagonal and not a corner.

     The radius is bounded by the tab, not by the body. The tab has 3.7 units of top edge to spend,
     and once the corner takes most of it there is no straight left and the tab reads as a bump.
     At 2.7 it keeps roughly twice the corner in flat edge; much past that it does not. -->
